  "body": "Deadline sale: Closes on Wednesday 2 December 2026 at 4:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nFrom the moment you step inside, 84 Mount Taylor Drive feels different. Light pours through, the finishes are crisp and considered, and every room leads you towards the outdoors.\r\n\r\nThe secret is the aspect. This home faces fully north, and bifold doors run down the entire side of the house, so sunshine fills the ground floor from morning to evening. Under 2.7-metre ceilings, the lounge, family room, dining, and kitchen flow together, bright and airy in every season.\r\n\r\nOpen the bifolds and the living spaces spill onto a private patio, hedged in green and covered by a large pergola. There’s an outdoor fireplace/pizza oven for cool evenings and relaxed weekend feasts, a spa for winding down, and room for a long table full of friends. Summer entertaining, sorted.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen is sleek and sophisticated, with a dark granite bench, pendant lighting, and plenty of room for the barstools to fill up. Plantation shutters and soft neutral tones keep everything calm and bright. A second living space with a gas fireplace and plush carpet gives the household somewhere to spread out or retreat.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, four bedrooms surround a generous landing that’s yours to use however you like: a rumpus room, a second TV room, a homework zone, or a home office. The master suite is a true retreat, with a walk-in wardrobe and a newly renovated ensuite with a glass shower  and a brushed brass rain shower head. The family bathroom has been given the same polished update and adds a freestanding bath, perfect for a long soak at the end of the day.\r\n\r\nDownstairs also offers a handy powder room, a home office (or fifth bedroom) opening to a front deck, a laundry, and internal access to the double garage.\r\n\r\nCrossfield Reserve is just down the road, Glendowie Primary and Glendowie College are close by, and Te Taurere (Taylor Hill) watches over the neighbourhood. It’s an easy, lovely place to raise a family.\r\n\r\n\r\nHighlights:\r\n\r\n• Full north-facing aspect with sun all day\r\n\r\n• Bifold doors the entire length of the house to a private patio\r\n\r\n• Floor size approx 238m2\r\n\r\n• 2.7 metre stud on the lower level\r\n\r\n• Private patio with large pergola, outdoor fireplace/pizza oven, and spa\r\n\r\n• 4 bedrooms plus office or 5th bedroom\r\n\r\n• Flexible upstairs landing for a rumpus, TV room, or office\r\n\r\n• 2.5 bathrooms: updated ensuite and family bathroom with a freestanding bath, plus a downstairs powder room\r\n\r\n• Two living areas, one with a gas fireplace\r\n\r\n• Crossfield Reserve just down the road, with Glendowie Primary and College close by\r\n\r\n•  Internal-access double garage plus off-street parking\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
